00:28:25.247 --> 00:28:26.540
My birthday week is coming up.

472
00:28:26.623 --> 00:28:28.876
and I expect a really thoughtful
and expensive gift.

473
00:28:28.959 --> 00:28:31.879
- There's no birthday week.
- Yes. It's the week of your birthday.

474
00:28:31.962 --> 00:28:33.547
You're not a 16th-century monarch.

475
00:28:33.630 --> 00:28:37.259
You can't command multiple days
for your personal festivities.

476
00:28:37.342 --> 00:28:39.136
Remember our Monopoly tournaments?

477
00:28:39.219 --> 00:28:41.930
Well. I need a Get Out Of Jail Free card.

478
00:28:42.931 --> 00:28:46.685
Anyway. last night. it was rough.

479
00:28:47.686 --> 00:28:49.771
I wish I could talk to you about it.

480
00:28:50.772 --> 00:28:51.607
Bye.

481
00:28:53.483 --> 00:28:55.027
Lucy.

482
00:28:56.445 --> 00:28:57.613
Nick?

483
00:28:57.696 --> 00:28:58.906
Can I come in?

484
00:28:59.907 --> 00:29:04.036
No. No. no. no. Lucy is dead.

485
00:29:04.119 --> 00:29:05.746
How'd she die?

486
00:29:05.829 --> 00:29:08.081
- Decapitated on a roller coaster.
- That's a shame.

487
00:29:08.165 --> 00:29:09.958
She had such a nice head.

488
00:29:13.212 --> 00:29:15.005
And you are not wearing any pants.

489
00:29:17.424 --> 00:29:20.010
Pants. No. Not wearing those.

490
00:29:21.970 --> 00:29:23.555
Shoelaces in a bag?

491
00:29:24.556 --> 00:29:26.266
Go ahead. Judge me.

492
00:29:26.350 --> 00:29:27.976
No judgments.

493
00:29:28.060 --> 00:29:32.481
- Wait. What are you doing here?
- I wanna show you something. Come on.

494
00:29:32.564 --> 00:29:34.900
- How did you get in here?
- Your roommates let me in.

495
00:29:34.983 --> 00:29:37.027
Those bitches.

496
00:29:44.451 --> 00:29:48.664
Okay. So this map was just here
when you showed up this morning?

497
00:29:48.747 --> 00:29:50.791
- Yep.
- Who could have left it?

498
00:29:50.874 --> 00:29:53.877
I know a construction worker.
a delivery guy.

499
00:29:53.961 --> 00:29:56.839
one of your multiple personalities?

500
00:29:56.922 --> 00:29:58.423
This is amazing.

501
00:29:58.507 --> 00:30:03.971
There are broken people out there like me.
people who need to let go and move on.

502
00:30:04.054 --> 00:30:07.182
Good. Well. you can take the stuff
and move on.

503
00:30:07.266 --> 00:30:11.228
There's nowhere else like this.
I wish someone had done this for me.

504
00:30:11.311 --> 00:30:13.897
The Broken Heart Gallery could be
a community service.

505
00:30:13.981 --> 00:30:15.274
No. This is my hotel.

506
00:30:15.357 --> 00:30:19.820
It is not some sort of Lost and Found
for hoarder stalkers.

507
00:30:19.903 --> 00:30:21.947
- Again. not a hoarder.
- Hoarder.

508
00:30:22.030 --> 00:30:23.740
No. We've been through this.

509
00:30:23.824 --> 00:30:26.535
Oh. wow. this is the shrine to exes
you were talking about?

510
00:30:26.618 --> 00:30:27.870
I didn't say... I...

511
00:30:27.953 --> 00:30:29.913
- It's a direct quote.
- I didn't say that.

512
00:30:29.997 --> 00:30:31.707
Lucy. this is my friend Marcos.

513
00:30:31.790 --> 00:30:33.876
Hey. Oh. my God. We're friends now?

514
00:30:33.959 --> 00:30:37.421
That would explain why I'm building
a bar top for you for free.

515
00:30:37.504 --> 00:30:39.923
- Can you not...? Don't listen to him.
- Friendship. Servitude.

516
00:30:40.007 --> 00:30:42.968
I am the godfather to his unborn child.

517
00:30:43.051 --> 00:30:46.221
No. he's lobbying
for the position of godfather.

518
00:30:46.305 --> 00:30:50.058
Plot twist: It's not going well.
If I had to guess. you know?

519
00:30:50.142 --> 00:30:52.603
Would you want this man
to be your spiritual guide?

520
00:30:52.686 --> 00:30:54.980
No. Maybe my TV guide.

521
00:30:55.063 --> 00:30:56.899
- Am I right?
- Terrible dad joke.

522
00:30:56.982 --> 00:30:58.400
I like her. Let's get to work.

523
00:30:58.483 --> 00:30:59.610
- Okay.
- Nice to meet you.

524
00:30:59.693 --> 00:31:02.237
Wait. Wait. wait. wait.

525
00:31:02.321 --> 00:31:04.448
I can help. I...

526
00:31:05.449 --> 00:31:08.118
I can help with the hotel
in exchange for gallery space.

527
00:31:08.202 --> 00:31:09.661
- No.
- No. I can help.

528
00:31:09.745 --> 00:31:15.083
I can... I can paint. I can saw.
I can lift and lay tile. grout.

529
00:31:15.167 --> 00:31:16.793
- Is that...? That's a thing.
- Yeah.

530
00:31:16.877 --> 00:31:18.128
It's not gonna happen.

531
00:31:18.212 --> 00:31:22.674
That sounds like free labor.
and. Nick. you love free labor. don't you?

532
00:31:22.758 --> 00:31:23.675
You do. Come on.

533
00:31:23.759 --> 00:31:26.094
- Come on.
- You don't have a plan for the balcony yet.

534
00:31:26.178 --> 00:31:30.057
I did say I had a plan for the balcony.
I said it was phase two.

535
00:31:30.140 --> 00:31:32.601
Sorry. balconies are really important.

536
00:31:32.684 --> 00:31:34.102
- He gets it.
- They're essential.

537
00:31:34.186 --> 00:31:36.522
- What is going on?
- Two people agreeing.

538
00:31:36.605 --> 00:31:39.608
- Maybe eternal friendship. I don't know.
- We're bonding. We're friends?

539
00:31:39.691 --> 00:31:41.485
We should take it step by step. but sure.

540
00:31:41.568 --> 00:31:42.986
- Okay.
- It's a good start.

541
00:31:43.070 --> 00:31:44.988
- I hate both of you.
- Is that a yes?

542
00:31:45.072 --> 00:31:46.573
- No. No.
- Hell. yes.

543
00:31:46.657 --> 00:31:49.660
Of course. We could use the help.
You start tomorrow. 7 in the morning.

544
00:31:49.743 --> 00:31:52.287
Get us the coffee. right?
You know. gotta pay the piper.

545
00:31:52.371 --> 00:31:55.582
We do love oat milk. You can get almond milk
if you don't have it.

546
00:31:55.666 --> 00:32:00.045
Soy milk. whatever. Have fun with it.
But nothing with actual dairy.

547
00:32:00.128 --> 00:32:01.839
He gets really sensitive in his tummy.

548
00:32:01.922 --> 00:32:04.842
- Okay. All right. Let's...
- He has IBS. it's embarrassing.

549
00:32:04.925 --> 00:32:06.343
- IBS is a real thing.
- Stop it.

550
00:32:06.426 --> 00:32:09.721
- Tell me more about his tummy.
- This is not happening. There is no tummy.

551
00:32:09.805 --> 00:32:11.139
Goodbye.

552
00:32:11.223 --> 00:32:13.517
- Dude. What? No.
- We have 30 days. We need help.

553
00:32:52.472 --> 00:32:54.141
This is Morris.

554
00:32:54.224 --> 00:32:56.476
My husband and I got him together.

555
00:32:56.560 --> 00:32:57.895
My husband left.

556
00:32:58.896 --> 00:33:01.190
Morris took it pretty hard.

557
00:33:02.191 --> 00:33:04.568
Yeah. he died immediately.

558
00:33:06.111 --> 00:33:10.991
Let me get this straight. You are collecting
other people's junk in addition to your own?

559
00:33:12.409 --> 00:33:15.370
Oh. shut up. Jeff.
I should text Max about this.

560
00:33:15.454 --> 00:33:17.748
- He likes to be up to date with galleries.
- No.

561
00:33:17.831 --> 00:33:20.167
- Don't do that.
- You're right. I'll slide in the DMs.

562
00:33:20.250 --> 00:33:22.586
- That's more chill.
- You need to get a grip.

563
00:33:22.669 --> 00:33:24.963
He is dating a doctor
with the face of an angel.

564
00:33:25.047 --> 00:33:26.381
You're a monster.

565
00:33:26.465 --> 00:33:29.551
Thank you.
Okay. you need some sexual Listerine.

566
00:33:29.635 --> 00:33:30.969
Jeff agrees.

567
00:33:31.053 --> 00:33:33.847
What about that new guy. Nick?

568
00:33:33.931 --> 00:33:37.935
Last time I slept with someone
I worked with. it ended very badly.

569
00:33:38.018 --> 00:33:40.521
Oh. my God. That is so true. Jeff.
That does sound like progress.

570
00:33:40.604 --> 00:33:41.438
Thank you.

571
00:33:41.522 --> 00:33:44.942
Why don't you invite your "friend" Nick
to my birthday?

572
00:33:45.025 --> 00:33:47.986
I came up with a new theme. murder karaoke.

573
00:33:48.070 --> 00:33:50.072
It combines my favorite things.
murder and karaoke.

574
00:33:50.155 --> 00:33:51.990
- A heavenly combo.
- A perfect combination.

575
00:33:52.074 --> 00:33:54.451
You guys.

576
00:33:54.535 --> 00:33:56.245
I am in love.

577
00:33:56.328 --> 00:33:59.915
Her name is Irina. and she's got
tiny baby bones like a baby chick.

578
00:33:59.998 --> 00:34:03.752
and I just wanna build a nest for her
and chew her food for her and feed her.

579
00:34:03.836 --> 00:34:05.462
Jesus. I give it two weeks.

580
00:34:05.546 --> 00:34:09.007
Do I detect cynicism
from the great believer of love?

581
00:34:09.091 --> 00:34:11.927
She's right. You've banged
more Russian models than a tech billionaire.

582
00:34:12.010 --> 00:34:14.137
- If you were a guy. we would hate you.
- Yeah.

583
00:34:14.221 --> 00:34:15.764
- I don't need this.
- Yes. you do.

584
00:34:15.848 --> 00:34:19.893
- No. I don't. No. I don't. Okay.
- Yes. you do. Eat the pasta.

585
00:34:23.355 --> 00:34:25.774
Hey. Nick. I...

586
00:34:26.775 --> 00:34:29.695
- I can't work anymore this week. dude.
- Why?

587
00:34:29.777 --> 00:34:35.117
Your homeboy's been commissioned to build
a new table for that hotel in Fort Green.

588
00:34:35.199 --> 00:34:37.661
Really? That place is so cheesy.

589
00:34:37.744 --> 00:34:40.956
Oh. my God. How dare I take their money
when you don't like their mason jars.

590
00:34:41.039 --> 00:34:42.708
Look. man. I know...

591
00:34:42.791 --> 00:34:46.043
I know things are tough.
but I have a meeting at the bank on Friday.

592
00:34:46.128 --> 00:34:48.045
and I will get you your money.

593
00:34:48.130 --> 00:34:50.549
- You are first on my list.
- Oh. there's a list?

594
00:34:50.632 --> 00:34:52.759
Can I see the list. or...?

595
00:34:52.842 --> 00:34:55.262
- It's a theoretical list. Nick...
- It's gonna happen.

596
00:34:55.344 --> 00:34:57.472
- Come on.
- I can't keep doing this. man.

597
00:34:57.556 --> 00:35:01.310
I got a family. All right?
I have responsibilities. I'm sorry.

598
00:35:02.311 --> 00:35:04.646
Don't shut off on me. I...

599
00:35:04.730 --> 00:35:06.440
Show me those blushy cheeks.

600
00:35:06.523 --> 00:35:09.401
Oh. my God. I just feel so warm inside
when I see them. Show me...

601
00:35:09.484 --> 00:35:11.695
I'm fine. man. Please. just go. okay?

602
00:35:11.778 --> 00:35:13.363
All right.

603
00:35:13.447 --> 00:35:16.825
Good morning. building buds!
Who's ready to work?

604
00:35:16.909 --> 00:35:18.327
Because I am. Check me out.

605
00:35:18.410 --> 00:35:20.996
Look at this belt.
a practical belt for tools.

606
00:35:21.997 --> 00:35:24.917
- Here is your coffee. Marky Mark.
- All right. Lucy Liu.

607
00:35:25.918 --> 00:35:29.338
- And then. for you. I got the special milks.
- Thank you.

608
00:35:30.339 --> 00:35:31.381
- Dude.
- Sorry.

609
00:35:31.465 --> 00:35:35.469
Her Majesty looks a little upset
this morning. so tread lightly.

610
00:35:35.552 --> 00:35:39.765
Oh. no. We need to talk about our feelings?
Because the CFO has arrived.

611
00:35:39.848 --> 00:35:41.683
Chief Feelings Officer is here.

612
00:35:41.767 --> 00:35:45.145
- Let's hold hands. Okay. bring it in. guys.
- God. Dad jokes. Okay. I'm out.

613
00:35:45.229 --> 00:35:46.355
- See you. dude.
- Bye.

614
00:35:48.023 --> 00:35:49.983
- Who is that?
- Yeah. you're in the right place.

615
00:35:51.026 --> 00:35:52.945
- Hi.
- Hey.

616
00:35:53.946 --> 00:35:57.824
- Are you here for the Broken Heart Gallery?
- Yeah. Is this that heartbreak thing?

617
00:35:57.908 --> 00:36:01.161
Yeah. You're in the right place.
Welcome. I'm Lucy. head curator.

618
00:36:01.245 --> 00:36:02.829
Yeah. Willhelmina.

619
00:36:02.913 --> 00:36:04.915
So how's this whole thing work?

620
00:36:04.998 --> 00:36:07.835
I don't know.
How does this whole thing work?

621
00:36:07.918 --> 00:36:12.214
Well. why don't you we start
by you telling me what you brought and why?

622
00:36:12.297 --> 00:36:16.635
Yeah. Well. met my ex. Gina.
while I was actually...

623
00:36:16.718 --> 00:36:17.803
Oh. wait. Pause.

624
00:36:17.886 --> 00:36:20.097
Do you mind if I record this?

625
00:36:20.180 --> 00:36:22.766
- Just. you know. for our socials.
- Yeah. Sure.

626
00:36:22.850 --> 00:36:24.434
Take a step back against this.

627
00:36:24.518 --> 00:36:26.228
- Right. Here?
- Ooh. that is perfect.

628
00:36:26.311 --> 00:36:27.771
And go.

629
00:36:27.855 --> 00:36:29.356
I was in the hospital.

630
00:36:29.439 --> 00:36:32.192
I was recovering
from a pretty nasty skydiving accident.

631
00:36:32.276 --> 00:36:35.779
She was my nurse
and had a body cast covered all my tats.

632
00:36:35.863 --> 00:36:38.323
so Gina. she drew these ones on for me.

633
00:36:38.407 --> 00:36:40.367
When I could walk. I asked her to marry me.

634
00:36:40.450 --> 00:36:42.536
But then she changed her mind
three weeks later.

635
00:36:42.619 --> 00:36:44.788
- No.
- Damn. Gina.

636
00:36:44.872 --> 00:36:46.373
Anyway. time passed.

637
00:36:46.456 --> 00:36:51.211
but this just sat in the corner
of my bedroom. taunting me.

638
00:36:51.295 --> 00:36:56.758
- How long have you held on to it for?
- Six... Five years. Five years.

639
00:36:56.842 --> 00:37:00.846
Feels good to admit that. you know?
Then I heard about this place. so...

640
00:37:00.929 --> 00:37:03.515
And how exactly did you hear
about this place?

641
00:37:03.599 --> 00:37:06.685
- My masseuse's Instagram.
- And how did your masseuse hear about it?

642
00:37:06.768 --> 00:37:09.688
Don't listen to him.
Are you ready to hand it over?

643
00:37:09.771 --> 00:37:12.399
- Yeah. Yeah. I'm ready.
- Okay.

644
00:37:13.400 --> 00:37:15.152
It has an odor.

645
00:37:15.235 --> 00:37:16.904
Okay.

646
00:37:16.987 --> 00:37:18.363
- You did it.
- I did it.

647
00:37:18.447 --> 00:37:19.740
How does it feel?

648
00:37:19.823 --> 00:37:24.786
This is the first time in. like. five years
that I feel a little lighter.

649
00:37:24.870 --> 00:37:26.330
- Really?
- Yeah.

650
00:37:26.413 --> 00:37:29.208
That's amazing. Thank you.

651
00:37:29.291 --> 00:37:32.628
If you ever wanna see this again.
you can visit any time.

652
00:37:32.711 --> 00:37:34.713
- It'll be in my care. right here.
- Okay.

653
00:37:34.796 --> 00:37:37.716
Or. perhaps. at another location.

654
00:37:37.799 --> 00:37:40.385
No. definitely at this location.
Don't worry about him.

655
00:37:40.469 --> 00:37:43.388
- Who is he?
- Just one last thing.

656
00:37:43.472 --> 00:37:46.058
We just ask for a small donation.

657
00:37:46.141 --> 00:37:48.519
- Just to keep the gallery going.
- Yeah. yeah. yeah.

658
00:37:48.602 --> 00:37:51.772
There you go. It's only 5 bucks.
It's all I have.

659
00:37:51.855 --> 00:37:53.357
- Perfect.
- All right.

660
00:37:53.440 --> 00:37:55.067
Thank you so much.

661
00:37:57.194 --> 00:37:58.654
We're in business. baby.

662
00:37:58.737 --> 00:38:02.366
And Bonus Jonas. I'm making you clams.

663
00:38:03.992 --> 00:38:05.994
I'm going to take this.

664
00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:13.210
Thing about breakups is.

665
00:38:13.293 --> 00:38:15.963
someone can ruin your life
just by disappearing. you know?

666
00:38:16.046 --> 00:38:19.174
And then you hang on to the hope
that they'll barrel through your door

667
00:38:19.258 --> 00:38:22.761
full of believable explanations
as to why they didn't actually ghost you.

668
00:38:22.845 --> 00:38:25.806
or lose your number.
or just stop loving you.

669
00:38:25.889 --> 00:38:29.810
So what my ex left was a jar
of organic Choconut.

670
00:38:29.893 --> 00:38:33.272
So. heartbroken.
I would spoon it little by little

671
00:38:33.355 --> 00:38:36.650
while listening to Michael Bolton's
"When I'm Back On My Feet Again."

672
00:38:36.733 --> 00:38:38.235
It's rancid now.

673
00:38:38.318 --> 00:38:41.530
Kind of like my ex-girlfriend's soul.
I hate you. Just kidding.

674
00:38:41.613 --> 00:38:42.739
I hope you die.

675
00:38:42.823 --> 00:38:44.032
How do you get over someone?

676
00:38:44.116 --> 00:38:46.869
You just press some button on your body
and morph into a cyborg?

677
00:38:46.952 --> 00:38:50.163
Just keep going.
Don't look back. don't dwell on anything.

678
00:38:50.247 --> 00:38:52.291
Okay. so you just bottle everything up

679
00:38:52.374 --> 00:38:55.294
until you implode
in a fiery act of self-destruction?

680
00:38:55.377 --> 00:38:58.422
No. I manage my expectations.

681
00:39:04.845 --> 00:39:06.263
Marcos took another job.

682
00:39:06.346 --> 00:39:09.308
Our interior designer quit last week.
but I'm fine.

683
00:39:09.391 --> 00:39:10.893
I'm not upset. Why?

684
00:39:10.976 --> 00:39:15.355
Because I saw it coming a mile away
and I managed my expectations.

685
00:39:15.439 --> 00:39:20.152
Okay. so you don't ask anything of anyone.
which is why you're not asking me right now.

686
00:39:21.153 --> 00:39:24.239
- Asking you what?
- I'll be your interior designer.

687
00:39:24.323 --> 00:39:25.574
- Come on!
- Good God.

688
00:39:25.657 --> 00:39:28.785
Designer is just a fancy word for curator.
Or it's the other way around.

689
00:39:28.869 --> 00:39:31.788
I don't know. but regardless.
there's cool stuff all around us.

690
00:39:31.872 --> 00:39:33.790
You just need someone
to help you look for it.

691
00:39:33.874 --> 00:39:37.336
<i>Okay. but cool stuff means expensive.
and I'm pretty much broke.</i>

692
00:39:37.419 --> 00:39:41.340
<i>The key to collecting is seeing value
where others usually don't.</i>

693
00:39:41.423 --> 00:39:44.051
<i>You know. one lady's trash is
another lady's treasure.</i>

694
00:39:44.134 --> 00:39:45.552
<i>Kind of like relationships.</i>

695
00:39:45.636 --> 00:39:48.388
<i>And where might one find these treasures?</i>

696
00:39:48.472 --> 00:39:49.723
<i>Well. it is moving day.</i>

697
00:39:49.806 --> 00:39:51.975
First day of the month.
leases start and end.

698
00:39:52.059 --> 00:39:55.646
so New Yorkers are leaving pure gold
out on these streets.

699
00:39:55.729 --> 00:39:58.524
She's cute. she's charming.
she's calling my name.

700
00:39:58.607 --> 00:40:02.402
- She looks like rats live inside of her.
- Then she's habitable.

701
00:40:02.486 --> 00:40:06.073
Lucy. it's 40 blocks to the Chloe.
We are... We're not walking.

702
00:40:07.074 --> 00:40:09.660
Welcome to the nonviolent firearms show.

703
00:40:09.743 --> 00:40:10.661
Oh. my God.

704
00:40:10.744 --> 00:40:13.747
How do I seem to find myself
in this predicament?

705
00:40:18.293 --> 00:40:20.838
I'm tired. Can we take a break?

706
00:40:20.921 --> 00:40:23.131
Absolutely not. This was your idea.

707
00:40:23.215 --> 00:40:26.343
Fine. but can you distract me?
Tell me your life story.

708
00:40:26.426 --> 00:40:28.428
- My life story?
- Yeah.

709
00:40:28.512 --> 00:40:30.180
But my life hasn't even happened yet.

710
00:40:30.264 --> 00:40:33.141
Don't you ever think about
what you're gonna tell your biographer?

711
00:40:34.142 --> 00:40:37.563
- Is that something you think about?
- All the time. It'll begin as such:

712
00:40:37.646 --> 00:40:39.815
"It all started
on a sticky August afternoon."

713
00:40:39.898 --> 00:40:42.693
Oh. my God. Lucy. stop. Stop it.

714
00:40:42.776 --> 00:40:45.654
Okay. Your life story. Go.

715
00:40:46.655 --> 00:40:48.740
- Really?
- Yes.

716
00:40:50.450 --> 00:40:54.329
My parents really never settled down.
We moved a ton.

717
00:40:54.413 --> 00:40:56.081
That must have been hard.

718
00:40:56.164 --> 00:40:59.168
Think it make... Made me independent.

719
00:40:59.251 --> 00:41:01.712
So where would you go on holidays?

720
00:41:01.795 --> 00:41:03.422
Grandma's house.

721
00:41:04.423 --> 00:41:06.258
Tell me more about G-Ma.

722
00:41:06.341 --> 00:41:11.013
Well. she lived in this little place
called Kenosha. which is in Wisconsin.

723
00:41:11.096 --> 00:41:13.056
She looked like a Keebler elf.

724
00:41:13.140 --> 00:41:17.978
My grandma loved two things.
football and boxing.

725
00:41:18.061 --> 00:41:20.355
- She chewed tobacco till she was 90.
- Nice.

726
00:41:20.439 --> 00:41:23.108
And I always thought
she was this sweet old grandma.

727
00:41:23.192 --> 00:41:26.111
but it turns out
she was a bookie her entire life.

728
00:41:26.195 --> 00:41:29.323
- Okay. Grandma.
- I know. What a badass!

729
00:41:29.406 --> 00:41:33.076
After she died. they found
a wad of cash under her mattress.

730
00:41:34.077 --> 00:41:35.579
And she left it for me.

731
00:41:35.662 --> 00:41:38.624
- So that's what you used to start the Chloe.
- Yeah.

732
00:41:38.707 --> 00:41:41.627
And then you named it after her?
That's such a sweet tribute.

733
00:41:41.710 --> 00:41:44.588
- I didn't actually...
- Ice cream!

734
00:41:47.549 --> 00:41:48.926
Hey!

735
00:41:56.433 --> 00:41:59.520
<i>You know. we still haven't been
to the coolest little shop in Brooklyn.</i>

736
00:41:59.603 --> 00:42:02.147
<i>Only real insiders know about it.</i>

737
00:42:03.315 --> 00:42:05.484
<i>And what about you? Why New York?</i>

738
00:42:05.567 --> 00:42:07.319
I followed a man.

739
00:42:07.402 --> 00:42:09.780
Did the man know you were following him?

740
00:42:09.863 --> 00:42:13.617
He did when I snuck into his apartment.
impaled him with an ice pick

741
00:42:13.700 --> 00:42:15.786
and feasted on his remains.

742
00:42:15.869 --> 00:42:17.287
Frightening.

743
00:42:17.371 --> 00:42:19.790
But what's the real reason?

744
00:42:23.043 --> 00:42:27.589
Well. growing up. my mom was
an art history professor at Bard.

745
00:42:27.673 --> 00:42:30.342
So it was winter like 90 months of the year.

746
00:42:30.425 --> 00:42:34.012
So every weekend.
she'd take me to the Hessel Museum.

747
00:42:34.096 --> 00:42:40.310
And she taught me
that art tells stories about people. places.

748
00:42:40.394 --> 00:42:43.105
movements. moments in time.

749
00:42:45.190 --> 00:42:50.112
The coolest thing about my mom is.
she really sees art...

750
00:42:50.195 --> 00:42:53.031
in everything.

751
00:42:53.115 --> 00:42:55.033
Like. anywhere.

752
00:42:59.496 --> 00:43:02.249
What city has more art than New York?

753
00:43:07.546 --> 00:43:12.217
You know. I think this project is really
having a positive impact on me.

754
00:43:12.301 --> 00:43:14.595
I woke up this morning.
my pillow was totally dry.

755
00:43:14.678 --> 00:43:17.097
And then feel my bag. It's so light.

756
00:43:17.181 --> 00:43:21.018
I am growing too.
I have not called you a hoarder today.

757
00:43:21.101 --> 00:43:22.311
Typical man.

758
00:43:22.394 --> 00:43:24.980
Proud of himself for something
that isn't an achievement.

759
00:43:25.063 --> 00:43:27.774
Okay. Good talk. I'm gonna go get a coffee.

760
00:43:27.858 --> 00:43:29.318
Do you want anything?

761
00:43:29.401 --> 00:43:32.154
No. I quit coffee.
Only water or booze for this temple.

762
00:43:32.237 --> 00:43:33.989
I'm Paleo.

763
00:43:34.072 --> 00:43:38.493
- I'm not sure that's what Paleo means.
- No. no. It has to do with nuts.

764
00:43:38.577 --> 00:43:41.663
- Okay. I'm gonna go.
- Okay.

765
00:43:44.583 --> 00:43:46.084
- Hi there.
- Hi.

766
00:43:46.168 --> 00:43:49.630
I'm here for the 72-inch television.

767
00:43:49.713 --> 00:43:53.133
You guys are like
the last book shop on earth. huh?

768
00:43:53.217 --> 00:43:55.135
We're the real deal.
It was my grandfather's.

769
00:43:55.219 --> 00:43:58.931
Oh. okay. Well. I was about
to say something that...

770
00:43:59.014 --> 00:44:01.725
It wouldn't have gone well.
Anyway. thank you so much.

771
00:44:01.808 --> 00:44:04.144
- Have a great day.
- All right.

772
00:44:05.145 --> 00:44:09.566
- Oh. hey! Your case.
- I got it. I know him.

773
00:44:22.287 --> 00:44:24.081
Excuse me. Do you mind?

774
00:44:24.164 --> 00:44:26.750
Move! Oh. my God! Move.

775
00:44:27.751 --> 00:44:31.421
Excuse me. Do you have a moment
for Planned Parenthood? Okay.

776
00:44:31.505 --> 00:44:33.882
Excuse me. Do you have a moment
for Planned Parenthood?

777
00:44:33.966 --> 00:44:35.634
- Yes.
- Thanks.

778
00:44:35.717 --> 00:44:37.511
I gotta go.

779
00:44:37.594 --> 00:44:39.596
Do you have a moment for Planned Parenthood?

780
00:44:39.680 --> 00:44:42.307
Oh. you don't care
about reproductive rights?

781
00:44:46.562 --> 00:44:47.980
It's a first edition.

782
00:44:48.063 --> 00:44:50.399
- No.
- Yeah.

783
00:44:50.482 --> 00:44:52.067
Lucy!

784
00:44:54.152 --> 00:44:55.404
Max!

785
00:44:55.487 --> 00:44:57.155
Hi! Oh. my God.

786
00:44:57.239 --> 00:44:59.491
This is so random.

787
00:45:01.118 --> 00:45:01.952
Hi.

788
00:45:04.621 --> 00:45:05.998
- French.
- Oh. sorry.

789
00:45:06.081 --> 00:45:10.043
I just got back from Paris.
so still in there.

790
00:45:10.127 --> 00:45:12.754
- Right.
- This is Amelia.

791
00:45:12.838 --> 00:45:16.717
You saw her the night that...

792
00:45:16.800 --> 00:45:19.303
Are you okay? I'm a doctor. so...

793
00:45:19.386 --> 00:45:21.930
Me? Me? Me good. Me... I'm great.

794
00:45:22.014 --> 00:45:24.683
Because last time... You know.

795
00:45:26.435 --> 00:45:28.437
Right. That night. Oh. my God.

796
00:45:28.520 --> 00:45:29.646
That was such a fun night.

797
00:45:29.730 --> 00:45:32.858
I was just really living my truth
and. like. enjoying myself.

798
00:45:32.941 --> 00:45:34.318
I'm in my mid-20s.

799
00:45:34.401 --> 00:45:36.278
You know. I barely even wash my face.

800
00:45:36.361 --> 00:45:39.198
And sometimes I moisturize. if I feel fancy.

801
00:45:39.281 --> 00:45:42.117
But I just have the collagen
ready to go. I'm 26. so...

802
00:45:42.201 --> 00:45:44.328
Lucy! Hi.

803
00:45:44.411 --> 00:45:46.413
There you are.

804
00:45:47.456 --> 00:45:49.416
Got the flat white for you.

805
00:45:50.459 --> 00:45:53.629
- I...
- Yeah. I'm her assistant. Nick.

806
00:45:53.712 --> 00:45:55.881
- Hey. I'm Max.
- Hi.

807
00:45:55.964 --> 00:45:59.510
This one really knows
how to treat her staff. you know?

808
00:45:59.593 --> 00:46:01.720
- Staff?
- She didn't tell you?

809
00:46:01.803 --> 00:46:04.681
Lucy started her own gallery.

810
00:46:04.765 --> 00:46:08.185
Yeah. Big deal. I mean.
it's still underground. but it's gonna be...

811
00:46:09.186 --> 00:46:12.481
It's gonna blow up. Big. Big time.
Blowing. Lots of blowing up.

812
00:46:12.564 --> 00:46:14.274
That's...

813
00:46:14.358 --> 00:46:16.109
That's exceptional.

814
00:46:16.193 --> 00:46:18.862
Where is it? I'd love to come visit.

815
00:46:18.946 --> 00:46:22.533
And we would also love you
to come visit sometime.

816
00:46:22.616 --> 00:46:25.160
but we are late
for that meeting with that...

817
00:46:25.244 --> 00:46:28.747
- Meeting. Larry.
- Larry! Larry.

818
00:46:28.830 --> 00:46:30.249
Gagosian?

819
00:46:30.332 --> 00:46:31.333
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

820
00:46:31.416 --> 00:46:33.544
He's like a...
How did you describe him? Like a...

821
00:46:33.627 --> 00:46:36.004
Oh. he's like a post-modern teddy bear.

822
00:46:36.088 --> 00:46:38.257
- Just the sweetest guy.
- Yeah.

823
00:46:38.340 --> 00:46:39.550
You know?

824
00:46:39.633 --> 00:46:41.677
- Oh. yeah.
- Never met him.

825
00:46:41.760 --> 00:46:43.929
- We have to...
- Yeah. he hates it when we're late.

826
00:46:44.012 --> 00:46:45.389
- We should really run.
- He does.

827
00:46:45.472 --> 00:46:47.599
- But great to see you.
- Nice to meet you.

828
00:46:49.226 --> 00:46:51.353
Gagosian? Okay.

829
00:46:51.436 --> 00:46:53.063
Shit.

830
00:46:54.690 --> 00:46:56.900
He's just moved on. It's...

831
00:46:56.984 --> 00:46:59.528
Why is it so hard for me
and so easy for him?

832
00:46:59.611 --> 00:47:03.240
- Am I that forgettable?
- Are you kidding me? Max aches for you.

833
00:47:03.323 --> 00:47:07.327
He said so himself.
You're the wild card. the fun. the sparkle.

834
00:47:07.411 --> 00:47:11.248
- You think so?
- I... He thinks so.

835
00:47:11.331 --> 00:47:13.000
- Yes.
- Right.

836
00:47:14.001 --> 00:47:17.045
- Come on. Let's go in here.
- Okay.

837
00:47:18.046 --> 00:47:20.799
Do you think Max
and the doctor have moved in together?

838
00:47:20.883 --> 00:47:24.553
No. No. Max likes his personal space. so...

839
00:47:25.554 --> 00:47:28.974
She probably has an amazing
but crazy skin care routine.

840
00:47:29.975 --> 00:47:31.935
What if he likes it?

841
00:47:33.228 --> 00:47:34.813
Wait. where are we?

842
00:47:34.897 --> 00:47:37.441
Great. is this the third attempt at murder?

843
00:47:37.524 --> 00:47:40.944
Can we get it over and done with. please?
Just put me out of my misery.

844
00:47:41.028 --> 00:47:43.530
Hey. Yan. Do your thing.

845
00:47:53.874 --> 00:47:57.544
- What?
- I'll never tire of that reaction.

846
00:47:57.628 --> 00:48:00.464
- Yan.
- Hey. man. How's the hotel going?

847
00:48:00.547 --> 00:48:02.132
Excellent.

848
00:48:02.216 --> 00:48:04.635
Don't listen to her.
She's a glass-half-full kind of gal.

849
00:48:04.718 --> 00:48:08.847
You're right. yeah.
It's better to be a brooding cynic.

850
00:48:08.931 --> 00:48:11.475
Can you please go get my sign?

851
00:48:12.518 --> 00:48:14.561
So he just makes anything in neon?

852
00:48:14.645 --> 00:48:16.605
Yeah. including a blinking sign
over your head

853
00:48:16.688 --> 00:48:19.149
that says "Keep Back 200 Feet."

854
00:48:19.233 --> 00:48:23.737
Check this out. It's gonna look great
hanging in the lobby of the Chloe.

855
00:48:24.988 --> 00:48:29.910
It's Latin for "Into the middle of things."
It's what the hotel stands for.

856
00:48:29.993 --> 00:48:34.665
It's a place where people will meet
and intersect in our story.

857
00:48:35.749 --> 00:48:39.336
The Chloe will always be a place
they stopped along the way.

858
00:48:40.337 --> 00:48:43.507
See? I have feelings.

859
00:49:13.412 --> 00:49:16.665
Remember when I drove my car
into a parked school bus?

860
00:49:16.748 --> 00:49:19.835
Well. I'm not the mess you once knew.

861
00:49:19.918 --> 00:49:22.171
I have my shit together.

862
00:49:22.254 --> 00:49:23.630
Promise.

863
00:49:24.631 --> 00:49:27.801
- Hey. Who was that?
- No one.

864
00:49:27.885 --> 00:49:31.555
Oh. hello. fancy pants.
Where are you off to?

865
00:49:31.638 --> 00:49:34.391
Well. we are going to the bank.

866
00:49:34.474 --> 00:49:37.769
I have that meeting. and I am terrified.

867
00:49:37.853 --> 00:49:39.938
This is it. Make or break. right?

868
00:49:40.022 --> 00:49:43.567
- I'm coming along to play the race card.
- I think it'll be very effective.

869
00:49:43.650 --> 00:49:45.277
- Thank you.
- Look on the bright side.

870
00:49:45.360 --> 00:49:48.322
The gallery is bringing in
a bunch of revenue.

871
00:49:48.405 --> 00:49:51.867
No. I'm cautiously optimistic
in a very negative way.

872
00:49:51.950 --> 00:49:54.328
- I've lost all hope.
- But we should probably...

873
00:49:54.411 --> 00:49:56.330
Wait. wait. Before you go. take a seat.

874
00:49:56.413 --> 00:49:58.248
- I want you to listen to this.
- We're...

875
00:49:58.332 --> 00:50:01.251
No. come on. It'll just take a minute.
It'll be good for you.

876
00:50:01.335 --> 00:50:03.003
I need to share.

877
00:50:04.004 --> 00:50:06.131
"Dwayne and I met on New Year's Eve.

878
00:50:06.215 --> 00:50:07.966
We stole this bottle of champagne

879
00:50:08.050 --> 00:50:10.344
and resolved to drink it together
the next year.

880
00:50:10.427 --> 00:50:13.805
But Dwayne got sick
and next year never came.

881
00:50:13.889 --> 00:50:16.099
Lately. I've found myself drinking alone.

882
00:50:16.183 --> 00:50:20.229
but this is the one bottle
I can't bring myself to open."

883
00:50:20.312 --> 00:50:23.148
Nope. Nope!

884
00:50:24.900 --> 00:50:27.444
- Nick. are you crying?
- Why...?

885
00:50:27.528 --> 00:50:29.154
No. Why would I...? What?

886
00:50:29.238 --> 00:50:31.323
Why wouldn't you cry? Dwayne is dead. dude.

887
00:50:31.406 --> 00:50:34.159
They're about to drink a bottle together
and now he's a ghost.

888
00:50:34.243 --> 00:50:37.412
He didn't ghost him. He's an actual ghost.
Why would you do that to us?

889
00:50:37.496 --> 00:50:40.249
We said we're about to blackmail a man
into giving us money.

890
00:50:40.332 --> 00:50:42.543
I don't know. Crying's my favorite activity.

891
00:50:42.626 --> 00:50:44.628
- It's true. She's very good at it.
- Thank you.

892
00:50:44.711 --> 00:50:48.757
Last weekend we got together. and we just
re-enacted scenes from <i>The Notebook.</i>

893
00:50:48.841 --> 00:50:50.801
- I wrote you every day.
- Every day?

894
00:50:50.884 --> 00:50:53.804
- I wrote you every day!
- I never stopped thinking...

895
00:50:53.887 --> 00:50:58.934
As much as I admire this budding friendship.
we have to go because we are running late.

896
00:50:59.017 --> 00:51:00.394
Sure.

897
00:51:00.477 --> 00:51:02.354
- Upper hands. Okay.
- Marcos. let's go.

898
00:51:02.437 --> 00:51:04.857
- You got this. Good luck.
- I'm okay.

899
00:51:04.940 --> 00:51:08.151
April. 2006. Maxwell Desmond's bar mitzvah.

900
00:51:08.235 --> 00:51:11.238
So I show up and I do my best move for him.

901
00:51:12.239 --> 00:51:13.115
He was just kidding.

902
00:51:13.198 --> 00:51:16.159
He actually had gotten
an over-the-pants handy

903
00:51:16.243 --> 00:51:17.828
from Jenny Gluck that night.

904
00:51:18.829 --> 00:51:24.376
So I've kept this yarmulke
as a reminder that men can hurt you.

905
00:51:53.197 --> 00:51:54.448
"You're not a hoarder."

906
00:51:54.531 --> 00:51:57.618
"Thank you for saying that.
I do really appreciate that."

907
00:51:58.619 --> 00:52:00.621
"You hair looks great." "Yours does."

908
00:52:00.704 --> 00:52:02.456
"Thanking you..."

909
00:52:02.539 --> 00:52:05.334
Hi. Gallery donation?

910
00:52:05.417 --> 00:52:07.419
- Is Nick here?
- No.

911
00:52:07.503 --> 00:52:09.880
Just me. Us.

912
00:52:11.256 --> 00:52:12.090
Cool.

913
00:52:13.091 --> 00:52:16.094
Do you want me to tell him you stopped by?
Leave a message?

914
00:52:17.304 --> 00:52:18.180
No.

915
00:52:19.181 --> 00:52:20.724
Okay.

916
00:52:24.269 --> 00:52:26.104
See you later.

917
00:52:28.649 --> 00:52:31.026
"She kind of seemed like a bitch."

918
00:52:31.109 --> 00:52:33.820
"Stop. You can't say that. Go.

919
00:52:34.821 --> 00:52:36.448
No.

920
00:52:37.491 --> 00:52:39.910
No! Think about what you said."

921
00:53:09.690 --> 00:53:12.401
That was sweet but psycho.
Next up. we got Ben.

922
00:53:12.484 --> 00:53:14.528
"I Wanna Know What Love Is."

923
00:53:14.611 --> 00:53:17.865
Hi. thank you. guys.
so much for coming to my... Jeff.

924
00:53:17.948 --> 00:53:20.033
For coming to my birthday.

925
00:53:20.117 --> 00:53:22.452
I know this is a really important day
for all of us.

926
00:53:22.536 --> 00:53:25.289
and. you know.
as I was reflecting on my last 27 years.

927
00:53:25.372 --> 00:53:27.332
I was kind of thinking ahead to my death.

928
00:53:27.416 --> 00:53:28.959
- What is happening?
- Eyes up.

929
00:53:29.042 --> 00:53:32.546
And I was thinking that at my funeral.
I wanna be taxidermied

930
00:53:32.629 --> 00:53:35.424
and I want a photo booth
so people can come and take photos of me.

931
00:53:35.507 --> 00:53:38.177
And I'll have wine and hats
and different things.

932
00:53:38.260 --> 00:53:40.429
- What do you guys think of that?
- Inspired!

933
00:53:40.512 --> 00:53:43.473
- Happy birthday. Amanda!
- Happy birthday. Amanda.

934
00:53:43.557 --> 00:53:45.559
- How's it going?
- Hi!

935
00:53:45.642 --> 00:53:48.520
- I picked up your dead man cake...
- Oh. my God. thank you.

936
00:53:48.604 --> 00:53:50.105
...that you asked a stranger to get for you.

937
00:53:50.189 --> 00:53:52.816
This is my wife Randy
and that's my baby inside of her.

938
00:53:52.900 --> 00:53:55.569
Oh. my God. tell us everything
about being pregnant.

939
00:53:55.652 --> 00:53:58.113
Pretty terrible so far.

940
00:53:58.197 --> 00:54:01.533
Well. the making of it was fun.
